  "notes": "A legal term: the victim of a crime (or the victim's legal representative) formally asks the police or prosecutors to prosecute. Some crimes, the {親告罪|しんこくざい}, can be prosecuted only after such a complaint.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜⟦で→で：00502_de⟧{告訴|こくそ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to press charges for ~ (⟦{詐欺|さぎ}→詐欺：09789_sagi⟧, ⟦{名誉毀損|めいよきそん}→名誉毀損：17874_meiyokison⟧, ⟦{窃盗|せっとう}→窃盗：15280_settou⟧)\n- {告訴|こくそ}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{取|と}り{下|さ}げる: to drop the charges\n- {告訴状|こくそじょう}: written criminal complaint\n- ⟦{刑事|けいじ}→刑事：02741_keiji⟧{告訴|こくそ}: criminal complaint\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{告発|こくはつ}→告発：07999_kokuhatsu⟧: a criminal complaint filed by a third party, not the victim; also whistleblowing\n- ⟦{起訴|きそ}→起訴：10577_kiso⟧: indictment — the prosecutor's decision to take the case to court, which may follow a {告訴|こくそ}\n- ⟦{訴訟|そしょう}→訴訟：07642_soshou⟧: litigation, civil or criminal (⟦{刑事|けいじ}→刑事：02741_keiji⟧⟦{訴訟|そしょう}→訴訟：07642_soshou⟧); {告訴|こくそ} is the victim's criminal complaint that can start a case\n- ⟦{被害届|ひがいとどけ}→被害届：15706_higaitodoke⟧: a report of damage to the police, which does not itself ask for punishment",
